  "body": "The current version says (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#inert-subtrees):\r\n\r\n\"When a node is inert, then the user agent must act as if the node was absent for the purposes of targeting user interaction events, may ignore the node for the purposes of text search user interfaces (commonly known as \"find in page\"), and may prevent the user from selecting text in that node.\"\r\n\r\nIt says that no \"targeting user interaction events\", which sort of makes me assuming that inert subtrees can't receive focus, but I think it'd be better to spec that out clearly. This is also in sync with inert subtree use cases like modal HTML dialogs and HTML inert attribute which is used to add hidden but accessible elements.\r\n\r\nNot sure but having \"targeting user interaction events including focus events\" might be enough.\r\n",
